"First active","In service","First visit","First bought","25 destroyed","First kill","First downing","Taken in 5 runs","Grade 10","Cleared in weather at night","Bought 5 times","The enemy\'s riflemen, fighting as a squad. They move up from cover to cover and fire on the tank from medium range. On the Iron Tundra they come on skis.","Two-man anti-tank teams. They kneel, steady the launcher and fire a rocket that hits far harder than rifle fire.","The signaller who carries a squad\'s radio. While he\'s alive, the artillery\'s next barrage comes in sooner.",
"The enemy\'s main battle tank. It moves between firing positions, swings its turret onto the tank and fires heavy shells.","An infantry fighting vehicle: light armor and a quick-firing autocannon that fires in short bursts, moving often to keep you in sight.","An attack helicopter. It hovers at range, turns its nose toward the tank and fires volleys of rockets.","Explosive drones launched by BASTION. Each one flies straight at the tank and blows up on contact.","An anti-tank gun dug in behind sandbags. It can\'t move, but its shells hit hard, and the sandbags shield it from the front.",
"A mortar crew that sets up out of sight and lobs bombs onto the ground around the tank, a marker showing where each one will land.","An infantryman with a flamethrower. He closes in fast and sprays fire that keeps burning on the ground.","A field engineer who lays mines in the tank\'s path and patches up damaged enemy vehicles.","A marksman in an Altstadt window, aiming for the tank\'s vision slits. His shot doesn\'t touch the armor: it blinds the crew for a few seconds.","A turretless tank with a long fixed gun. It turns its whole hull to aim and fires one powerful shot. Its front armor is thick and its rear thin.",
"A fast, lightly armored scout car. It fires flares that mark the tank so the rest of the enemy can find it.","A halftrack mounting anti-aircraft guns. It goes after your drones and aircraft first; its rounds only scratch a tank.","A dive bomber. It makes several passes over the tank, a siren rising as it dives, and drops a line of bombs on each pass before it flies off.","An armored snow plow on the Iron Tundra. It comes in from the flanks or from behind and builds up speed to ram the tank.","Twin-gun volleys",
"A fan of shells","A charge that flattens cover","Calls in infantry","Chaingun sweeps","Rocket rain","Troop drops","Strafing runs","Missile volleys","Missile swarms","A railgun shot down a marked line","EMP bursts","Kamikaze drones","Gun cars fire broadsides","Mortar and rocket cars bombard","Troop cars drop squads","Flak, flame and mine cars","A fortress car shields its neighbours","A command car marks you","Attacks 30% faster, and the shell fan fires twice, the second covering the gaps.","Attacks 30% faster; rocket rain covers half as much ground again and the chaingun sweeps back across.",
"Attacks 30% faster; the railgun fires twice and every attack ends with an EMP pulse.","The train runs 40% faster and the locomotive\'s own guns join in.","VERDANT FRONT","GRASSLAND BATTLEFIELD","Rolling fields cut by trenches and tree lines. Push through the enemy screen and break their armoured spearhead.","t_grass","HOLLOW FIELDS","WAR-TORN FARMLAND","Burned barns, cratered crops and mud. Their gunship hunts from the smoke above the harvest.","t_farm","ALTSTADT","WAR-RUINED TOWN","A town ruined by war. Fight street by street to draw out BASTION.",
"SECRET FRONT - ENDLESS","The lost regiment\'s drums have led you to a frozen front that never ends. Hold the line.","t_snow","TRAINING GROUND","A fenced-off corner of the Verdant Front, kept for drills.","GOLIATH","REAPER","BASTION","JUGGERNAUT","SUPER-HEAVY TANK","HEAVY ATTACK GUNSHIP","MOBILE MISSILE FORTRESS","ARMOURED TRAIN","THE FULL GAME","THE CAMPAIGN","ENDLESS MAPS","PAINT SCHEMES","ESCALATION","ARMORY RANKS","WEEKLY OPERATIONS","The full game adds the campaign across three fronts and the secret fourth, weekly operations, four more vehicles, every Armory upgrade, medals, paint schemes, Escalation 1-10, and weather and night on every front.",
"Fight across the Verdant Front, Hollow Fields and Altstadt against GOLIATH, REAPER and BASTION, and whatever lies beyond them.","Hollow Fields, Altstadt and the Iron Tundra open for Endless in the full game.","Seven paint schemes per vehicle, each earned with its own challenge.","Ten levels of Escalation, from Hardened to Iron Rain, for every vehicle.","Extra rerolls every front, banishes every run, and Stand Down to switch off upgrades you don\'t want offered.","A new operation every week: the campaign on that week\'s seed, at Escalation 0 with the Depot off. Your best place on its board pays up to 10 REQ when the week ends.",
